      "message": "isKernelInRange is only used in test class and it can be private. \nthree arguments (target, from, to) likes the follows\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:cts/tests/tests/widget/src/android/widget/cts/HorizontalScrollViewTest.java;l\u003d967\n```\n    private boolean isInRange(int current, int from, int to) {\n        if (from \u003c to) {\n            return current \u003e\u003d from \u0026\u0026 current \u003c\u003d to;\n        }\n        return current \u003c\u003d from \u0026\u0026 current \u003e\u003d to;\n    }\n```\n\n\nIf we really want to get rid of isKernelInRange and isKernelAtLeast. Maybe we could do this way:\n\n1. implement isInRange() and isAtleast() in class Version\n```\npublic static class Version {\n    public boolean isInRange(final Version from, final Version to) {\n        return this.compareTo(from) \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 this.compareTo(to) \u003c 0;\n    }\n\n    public boolean isAtleast(final Version from) {\n        return this.compareTo(from) \u003e\u003d 0;\n    }\n```\n\n2. Invoke the isInRange() and isAtleast()\n```\nprivate static boolean isUdpOffloadSupportedByKernel(final String kernelVersion) {\n        DeviceInfoUtils.Version current \u003d DeviceInfoUtils.getMajorMinorSubminorVersion(kernelVersion);\n        \n        return current.isInRange(new Version(4, 14, 222), new Version(4, 19, 0))\n                || current.isInRange(new Version(4, 19, 176), new Version(5, 4, 0))\n                || current.isAtleast(new Version(5, 4, 98));\n    }\n\n```\n\naosp/2107827 has +2ed. If we go this way, maybe leave it as todo? because this refactor needs related tests as well",
